    "result_text": "All 274 tests pass, including `Cp13Tests`. \n\nThe change is implemented and green. Summary of what I added to enforce the daily owner-creation cap (400 when 20 owners already registered today):\n\n- **`CheckDailyOwnerLimit`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 new pipeline step that counts existing owners whose registration date matches the new owner's registration day and throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` once the count reaches 20.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 checked exception carrying the rejection message.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail`, consistent with the other handlers.\n- **`org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `checkDailyLimit` step (under `transaction` governance) into the pipeline, after the duplicate check and before city normalization.\n\nThe step is placed after `checkDuplicate` so a duplicate still returns 409; it runs before `save`, so the 21st create today is rejected with 400 without persisting anything.",
